{"id": "86235", "name": "משוואה ריבועית – פתרון בפירוק לגורמים, 2 סעיפים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "none", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Solve the following quadratic equation by factorising:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} = 0. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">a</span></div><p>Write this quadratic in factored form:</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ansf]] \\(=0\\).</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ansf]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:fac]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">b</span></div><p>Solve this equation, giving your answer as a set \\(\\left(\\mbox{e.g. }\\left\\{x_1 , x_2\\right\\}\\right)\\):</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\({{CT:1}} \\in \\) [[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Factorise the quadratic into two linear factors, then set each factor equal to zero.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Factorising (part a)</b><br>There are multiple ways of solving quadratic equations but if you can spot how to factorise the quadratic then this method is by far the fastest and simplest. In this example we can factorise the quadratic to give:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:2}} = 0. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Each factor equal to zero</b><br>Now, notice, that for the above equation to be equal to zero, the factors must be made to equal zero. So we find that:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:3}} = 0, \\]</p>or:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:4}} = 0. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The solution set (part b)</b><br>By rearranging these expressions we find that: \\({{CT:1}} = {{CT:5}}\\) or \\({{CT:1}} = {{CT:6}}\\). Therefore our solution set is:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}} \\in \\left\\{ {{CT:5}} , {{CT:6}} \\right\\}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "ansf", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "fac", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "FacForm", "sans": "ansf", "tans": "(cf1*v+a)*(cf2*v+b)", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "fac-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "fac-0-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — incorrect.</b> Write the quadratic as a product of two linear factors, and check by expanding the brackets.</div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "elementp(?,ans)", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Please replace \\(?\\) in the answer box with your answer and try again!</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "{ta1, ta2 }", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — incorrect.</b> Set each factor from part a equal to zero and solve for the variable.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "cf1", "cf2", "ta1", "ta2", "v"], "nvariants": 50}